DOF is a world-class offshore construction support, survey and IRM contractor. 
 DOF Canada is a leading provider of subsea services in all the major oil and gas production regions around the world. With world class ROVs (Remote Operated Vehicles), Survey systems, and a fleet of offshore construction vessels, the group combines expertise and technology to deliver integrated subsea solutions to the offshore oil and gas and renewable industries.
 DOF Canada is currently seeking a detailed oriented and client focused individual for the position of Intermediate Engineer . A key to success for this position is the ability to collaborate with offshore and onshore personnel. The Intermediate Engineer will report to the Project Technical/Engineering Manager and will receive day-to-day direction for activities such as analyses, reports/document reviews, tendering, design, etc. This position may have Offshore and/or International requirements. If you are looking for a dynamic environment to learn and grow your career, DOF Canada is a great opportunity!
 Key Responsibilities 
 Support DOF's core business initiatives and those of DOF's clients, Light Subsea Construction, Subsea Intervention, Decommissioning, Permanent Mooring Installation/Disconnection, Engineering Studies and Tenders) including lift rigging design and lift planning, equipment sea fastening design, and installation analyses specific to above core business initiatives;
 Ensures successful completion of the assigned project phase within the budgeted time and cost constraints, and within company policies;
 Help lead our regional effort to develop innovative solutions to client problems which support our core business;
 Support business development and tendering activities as required by management;
 Actively seek to develop safe, practical, cost effective and cutting edge solutions to project technical challenges;
 Promote the continual development of our HSEQ culture and system that minimizes the risk of injury to personnel, the environment and equipment to ALARP levels (As Low As Reasonably Practical);
 Promote the company’s organizational culture, values and reputation with all staff, customers, suppliers, partners and regulatory/official bodies;
 Encourage open communication between engineering and operations to create healthy productive culture;
 Diligently work towards meeting Regional and Departmental Key Performance Indicators (KPI’s);
 Execute all responsibilities according to lawful and ethical standards;
 Offshore work will be required
 Other engineering duties as directed by third parties in the case secondments.
