 Bachelor of Science degree in applicable engineering field of study (Civil, Mechanical, Ocean & Naval Architecture, Structural, or equivalent);
 Basic Survival Training (BST) would be an asset as there will be offshore work;
 Either working towards or has obtained a Professional Engineering licence;
 3-5 years’ experience subsea project/installation engineering experience;
 Familiar with procedural writing as it pertains to offshore ROV construction works.
 Experience related to the supervision of equipment System Integration Testing and functionality testing;
 Experience performing project vessel mobilizations and demobilizations;
 Offshore field experience related to the installation and decommissioning of subsea infrastructure;
 Knowledge of specialized software would be an asset (Example- Ansys/Inventor- Structural/Mechanical Engineers, Orcaflex- Hydrodynamics- Subsea Engineers, etc.);
 Knowledge of the marine environment and technical challenges associated with executing projects in these conditions;
